Certified Professional Program - New Building - To construct a new 5-storey commercial building consisting of: 

Storage Garage having vehicular access from the lane at level 1; Brewery (Group F, Division 2) at level 2; Office/Production Studio (Group D, Group F Division 2) at levels 3 and 4; and Office (Group D) at level 5.

Stage I (excavation/ shoring) issued April 22, 22

Stage II (foundation to grade) issued November 7/22

Stage III (full permit) issued August 31/23

Revision 1 (Issued April 3, 2025):
Change of CP from Michael Ferber to Marc Showers, P.Eng., CP effective March 6, 2025

Revision#2 (May 5, 2026) changes to the following:
-roof change from CLT to noncombustible OWSJ; 
- vertical service space removed;
- fire shutters for rear windows (exit exposure) due to high ceiling; 
- Unit 201 & 202 merged as one; public corridor for Unit 301 extends to connect directly to exit stair 3; 
- Units 401 & 402 merged as one (to match TI permits); 
- central storage changed to a washroom near Unit 201
- protection method for steel columns (change to gypsum board in some areas)

Certified Professional Program - New Building - To construct a new 34-storey noncombustible building consisting of:

-1st storey - entrance lobby, a rental office (unit#101), a theater &  storages;
-2 nd storey - amenity spaces (cowork space & a gym ), storages;
-3rd to 33th storeys -    275 secured rental housing;
-34th storey - amenity roof deck;

all over 5 levels of below grade parking. 

This building is provided with a radio antenna system. 

This is the NORTH SITE.
07- Nov-2023 - Stage I ( Excavation and Shoring)  issued.
02- May-2024  -Stage II (Foundation to Grade, struct. only) issued.
28-May-2024 - Stage III (Full permit) issued.

Revision#1 -  change of the Envelope Engineer’s company (Stantec acquisition of Morrison Hershfield) effective

Certified Professional Program - New Building - To construct a 6 storey with 69 Supportive Housing from 2nd to 6th floors with retails and residential ancillary uses on the main floor with no parking. Basement and main level are of concrete construction. Levels 2-6 are of wood frame construction. 
(No kitchen Exhaust ducts proposed. Only HVAC ducts at the main ceiling level.)

VBBL 2019 - Reviewed during 2020/2021 Pandemic.

STAGE 1 - Excavation and Shoring issued on April 14, 2021. 
STGAE 2 - Full Construction issued on June 25, 2021.
Rev# 1 (Apr. 21, 2022) - Interior and exterior changes on the following:

- changing from Affordable Housing to Supportive Housing;
- expanding the North retail unit;
- eliminating the South retail unit;
- expanding Amenity spaces with servery function, calming room and 
  security office at the first floor;
- reducing Class B bike stalls from 12 stalls to 8 stalls; and,
- adding a heat treatment room.

Rev# 2 - (Apr. 28, 2023) - Interior and exterior alterations and change of major occupancy per the following below and change of owners from Anhart Community to the City of Vancouver. 

- a change of use from Retail to Social Service Centre;
- changing Unit #210 from a 2 bedroom dwelling to ancillary office space
- updated interior details;
- removal of the Tensarch structure from the roof and addition of an 
  overhang, and;
- corrected Landscape drawing for Level 1 to show the correct mosaic tile 
  in the residential entry alcove.

High Density Housing / Commercial - New Building - To construct a six-storey multiple dwelling building containing 12 units (7 apartment units and 5 townhouse units), over one level of underground parking, having vehicular access from the lane.

*****This permit has been reviewed under the 2014 Vancouver Building By-law (#10908).*****

Permit Amendment #1- January 24th, 2022- S.Le
Refer to DP-2021-00713
•\tAlterations to combine two 5th floor units into a single unit;
•\tThe corridor between Stair 1/elevator and Stair 2 on the 5th floor 
        be removed and replaced with separate entry and exit corridors;
•\tTotal numbers of units decreased by 1 for a total of 11 units;
•\tIn suite storage decreased by one, affecting floor area;
•\tOverall FSR increased from 2.37 to 2.38;
•\tBicycle parking requirements decreased by 1 from 15 to 14;

High Density Housing / Commercial - New Building - **********PART 5 DESIGN***********
To construct a 3-storey residential building containing a total of three dwelling units, with a detached carport at the rear providing 3 parking spaces having vehicular access from the lane.

******THIS PERMIT HAS BEEN REVIEWED AND ISSUED UNDER THE REQUIREMENTS OF VBBL 2019***********

Building Review Branch Notes:
1. Sch. A, D, Arch. B, Geo. B, Struct. B are submitted. 
2. Entire building is sprinklered to NFPA 13D requirements.
3. All dwelling units have separate exterior entrances.
4. All new windows, doors, and skylights shall conform to AAMA/WDMA/CSA101/I.S.2/A440, NAFS.

Revision #1 related to DP-2025-00465 - June 4th, 2025
- remove attic floor windows on north elevation;
- add gable window addition on north elevation;
- change dormer window size on east and west elevation;
- reduce and relocate skylights;
- remove and add windows on east elevation;
- add tempered glass guardrail on north elevation;
- remove gable wall on north and south elevation;
- adjust main floor powder room of unit C; and
- remove wall for interior and bathroom on attic floor of unit A and B;

Revision #2 No DPMA required. Aug 12th, 2026
- in unit C - Showing the door swing of crawl space access hatch from powder room
- Change of applicant from Deepak Sharma to Johnny (Atul) Sharma, Property Owner.

High Density Housing / Commercial - New Building - *****PART 5 DESIGN *** 

To construct a new three storey multiple dwelling building containing three dwelling units with an accessory building and surface parking at the rear providing three parking spaces having vehicular access from the lane

Revision #1 (DPMA:DP-2024-00770) (April 16th , 2025):
1. Peak height increased by 0.06 ft. to 200.77 ft.;
2. Main floor ceiling height increased to 10 ft.;
3. Second floor ceiling height increased to 9 ft.;
4. Foundation plan and crawl space slab elevation revised;
5. Garage revised;
6. Main floor powder room layout and location revised for all 3 units;
7. Unit C main and second floor layout changed;
8. Third floor layout changed and added front & rear deck;
9. Added transparent glazing to front units entrance doors;
10. Added windows at north building elevation/main floor powder rooms;
11. Revised main floor south building elevation by shifting rear landings and stairs while revising proposed windows;
12. Revised main floor west building elevation windows;
13. Revised main floor windows from steel frame with wire glass to vinyl frame with tempered safety glass;
14. Proposed maneuvering at surface parking;
15. Updated impermeability and site coverage calculations and layouts;
16. Revised proposed roof;
17. Revised bicycle space location;
18. Revised unit A north facing window and unit B south facing window at main floor living room;

